WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.182
This video shows how to get a SWAT+ model
of

00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:06.180
a United States basin and add it to
SWATrust.

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.710
Open Set-up and look under the map.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.912
The page lists the basins of the data set
there,

00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:15.540
each with its code, its name and the size
of its download.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.158
Type the code of the basin, or a part of
its name,

00:00:19.158 --> 00:00:21.590
in the box Code or name above the list.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:25.840
For this video, type 11140204.

00:00:26.341 --> 00:00:29.651
Choose the form of the model with the two
buttons above the list.

00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:33.165
Basin alone leaves out the inflow from
upstream basins,

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.781
and With inflow from upstream brings in
their daily outflow.

00:00:36.981 --> 00:00:39.171
For this video, leave Basin alone.

00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:41.163
Click the row of the basin.

00:00:41.363 --> 00:00:44.589
The line under the list gives the size of
the download,

00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:47.463
the size on disk and the free space of
your disk.

00:00:47.966 --> 00:00:49.442
In the map of all basins,

00:00:49.442 --> 00:00:54.106
a click on a basin that is not among your
models marks its row in the same way.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:55.639
Click Download.

00:00:57.894 --> 00:01:00.114
The basin is added to the list Models.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:09.314
You can also add a model folder that you
already have: click Add a model folder.

00:01:09.514 --> 00:01:12.124
A dialog lists the folders of your
computer.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.810
Go to the folder of the model.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.090
Read the line at the foot of the dialog.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:31.820
For a model it says: This folder is a
model, it holds file.cio.

00:01:32.321 --> 00:01:33.591
Click Add this folder.

00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:41.359
The model is now in the list Models, and
it is chosen for the next run.

00:01:42.165 --> 00:01:44.585
Click the row of a model in the list
Models.

00:01:44.785 --> 00:01:47.845
The column Paths and period then shows
that model.

00:01:50.972 --> 00:01:54.222
The click on the row does not change which
models are chosen

00:01:54.222 --> 00:01:57.202
for the run; the tick at the left of the
row does that.

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:01.710
Under the list is the map.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:03.405
It opens on All basins,

00:02:03.405 --> 00:02:08.150
which shows the basins of the data set in
the conterminous United States.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:13.340
This basin draws the model in relief, with
its streams and a red dot at its outlet.

00:02:19.299 --> 00:02:20.716
In the map of all basins,

00:02:20.716 --> 00:02:24.286
a click on a basin of yours ticks its
model in the list Models,

00:02:24.286 --> 00:02:26.439
and a second click takes the tick out.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.700
A basin that lies below another basin
receives the flow of that basin.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.315
In a model, this flow enters at an inlet,

00:02:36.315 --> 00:02:39.790
and a point-source file of the model gives
it for each day.

00:02:44.117 --> 00:02:51.137
For the basin 11140204, the block of the
model shows two lines above Model folder.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:56.081
The line No inflow at 1 inlet says that an
inlet has no inflow data,

00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.407
so its inflow is 0.

00:02:57.907 --> 00:03:00.163
The line Inflow from upstream gives the

00:03:00.163 --> 00:03:02.824
number of inlets and the size of the
download,

00:03:02.824 --> 00:03:05.137
and the button Download stands under it.

00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:08.709
In a run, each inlet takes the first
source that it has.

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:12.742
SWATrust runs the model of the basin
upstream first when that

00:03:12.742 --> 00:03:16.449
model is in the list of models and an
inlet needs its flow.

00:03:16.949 --> 00:03:21.519
Add the folder of the model upstream with
Add a model folder, and take its tick out.

00:03:34.081 --> 00:03:34.891
Click Run.

00:03:35.091 --> 00:03:39.341
The line Upstream models under Checks
before the run counts these models.

00:03:42.769 --> 00:03:43.949
Click Start the run.

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:49.686
During the run, the table of the basins
lists an upstream model with the

00:03:49.686 --> 00:03:52.894
line Upstream of and the name of the model
that it feeds.

00:03:53.094 --> 00:03:56.444
The model below waits until the upstream
model has ended.

00:04:13.966 --> 00:04:17.570
SWATrust also writes a file README.txt
into the

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:21.636
folder of each basin of a run whose model
has inlets.

00:04:21.836 --> 00:04:24.009
The file has one line for each inlet,

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:26.946
and the line names the source that the
inlet took.

00:04:27.446 --> 00:04:31.760
If a model uses a part of SWAT+ that this
version does not include,

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.786
the engine does not run it, and Set-up
says so.

00:04:35.286 --> 00:04:39.536
The next chapter, Run your own model, adds
a model that you built yourself.
